   239	
   240	## User preferences
   241	
   242	- when planning small feature slices, the user said "`.dev/plan/001-minimal-hardcoded-agent.md` 정도로 적어두면 되지 않을까? 실행계획이잖아." -> for lightweight work, use an execution plan in `.dev/plan/` rather than over-specifying a big formal spec [Task 1]
   243	- when shaping early product scope, the user said "agent 하나만 두고 필요할 때 추가하자." -> default to the smallest workable slice and add complexity only when needed [Task 1]
   244	- when asking for backend/docs work, the user said "내가 작성하는 것보다 네가 작성을 하고 내가 검토할 거야." -> the agent should draft specs/docs for review rather than waiting for the user to author them first [Task 2]
   245	- when iterating on UI, the user wanted "간단하게 우선 만들고 실행해보자" and a `|채팅영역|디버깅영역|` split -> prefer a runnable first pass with explicit structure, then iterate visually [Task 3]
   246	- the user disliked gray input surfaces that looked disabled and preferred clearer, more professional UI states -> avoid ambiguous disabled-looking styling when the element is active [Task 3]
   247	- when asked if testing was done, the user wanted proof of effect, not only code changes or payload inspection -> verification should show user-visible behavior change, ideally in browser traces when the feature is UI-driven [Task 4]
   248	- the user kept removing vague copy such as "연결 없음" and "출처는 상단 탭" -> prefer explicit rows with concrete values over compressed legends or paraphrases of nearby UI [Task 5]
   249	
   250	## Reusable knowledge
   251	
   252	- `uv` had to be installed via Homebrew before `uv sync` and `uv run` worked; local MLX behaved better with `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=False`, and a preserved `messages` list is required for multi-turn CLI memory [Task 1]
   253	- For the chat API, SSE should use safe framing such as JSON or other line-safe payloads, and long-lived streams should not hold request-scoped DB sessions open after DB access is no longer needed [Task 2]
   254	- Local dev Postgres should be bound to `127.0.0.1:5432` for safety, and typed validation is preferred over raw dict handling in request schemas [Task 2]
   255	- Ant Design X is the preferred primitive set here for AI chat UI (`Bubble.List`, `Sender`, `ThoughtChain`), and the chat/debug layout works best as equal-height panes with independent scroll [Task 3]
   256	- The practical design-research path for this repo is official Ant Design token/Figma resources plus rendered screenshots, not feeding the whole antd repo into Claude Design [Task 3]
   257	- For node overrides, the strongest confidence comes from proving effect in both API-level verifiers and browser e2e: UI override applied, trace changes, tool-call count actually drops [Task 4]
   258	- The ToolTree can start collapsed, so browser tests must expand the correct branch before interaction or they will click the wrong target and misread the result [Task 4]
   259	- On detail pages, redundant legends are usually worse than explicit rows because the repo prefers one-source-of-truth terminology and direct placement of A2A / visibility / source information [Task 5]
   260	
   261	## Failures and how to do differently
   262	
   263	- Symptom: minimal CLI feels broken across turns. Cause: stateless loop dropped prior messages. Fix: preserve and resend the full `messages` history [Task 1]
   264	- Symptom: local MLX floods the stream with long reasoning output. Cause: Qwen thinking remained enabled. Fix: set `chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=False` for the minimal slice [Task 1]
   265	- Symptom: SSE/chat logic is fragile or unsafe. Cause: raw token text was streamed directly and validation stayed loose. Fix: use safe framing and typed schema validation, and close DB sessions before streaming when possible [Task 2]
   266	- Symptom: debug UI drifts out of sync or overwhelms the page. Cause: too much always-visible debug detail. Fix: use explicit panes and on-demand debug disclosure rather than a constant dump [Task 3]

